          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#brown_representability Brown representability
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
            says that for any reduced cohomology theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E^\bullet
            there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Omega-spectrum"} Omega-spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represents
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E^\bullet
            on pointed connected CW-complex
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
